+- [x] `install.sh`
+- [x] `package.nix`
+- [x] Unit tests
+- [x] README (en + zh-CN)
+- [x] `make`, `make check` (clang-format not installed on this machine; code
+  hand-matched to `.clang-format` — 4-space indent, brace on next line for
+  functions, ≤ 80 cols)
+- [x] Manual verification notes (below)
+- [x] Round 2: abort on denied authorization (D7); documented where polkitd
+  reads policies from (system profile on NixOS — the transient runtime
+  self-publish workaround was removed once that path was verified)
+
+## Verification notes
+
+Verified on the dev machine (polkit 127, uid 1000 `goll`, Wayland/GNOME):
+
+1. **Build/test (CI-equivalent):** `make -B all` + `make check` pass —
+   all unit tests (incl. 4 new `test_privilege` tests), `bash -n install.sh`,
+   `msgfmt --check` (0 untranslated, 0 fuzzy in `zh_CN.po`), and the new
+   policy-substitution/`xmllint` checks.
+2. **Install substitution:** `make install DESTDIR=<tmp> PREFIX=/usr/local`
+   produces `<tmp>/usr/local/share/polkit-1/actions/dev.seekey.policy`
+   with `…exec.path">/usr/local/bin/seekey<` (no `@BINDIR@` left).
+3. **`install.sh --dry-run --no-deps`:** policy install/remove lines appear
+   with the correct destination; existing udev flow untouched; `bash -n` OK.
+4. **No prompt for info modes:** with a fake `pkexec` first in `PATH`,
+   `seekey --print-config` / `--validate-config` never spawn it.
+5. **Correct elevation argv:** default mode (event nodes `root:input 0660`,
+   not a member → probe TRUE) spawns `pkexec <abs self> --seekey-restore-env=…`
+   with the allowlisted pairs (`WAYLAND_DISPLAY`, `DBUS_SESSION_BUS_ADDRESS`,
+   `XDG_RUNTIME_DIR`, …) followed by the original args; child exit status is
+   propagated to the parent.
+6. **Denial aborts (D7):** fake pkexec exiting 127 prints
+   `pkexec authorization was cancelled or denied; aborting` and seekey exits
+   with code 2 (no overlay starts); fake pkexec exiting 0 still propagates
+   exit status 0.
+7. **Drop failure is fatal, never continues as root:** under
+   `unshare -Ur` with `PKEXEC_UID=1000`, the drop path fails at
+   `initgroups()` and exits 2 with `seekey: failed to set up supplementary
+   groups: Operation not permitted`. `PKEXEC_UID` without euid 0 is a no-op.
+
+**Not verifiable on this machine** (needs a real polkit prompt / root):
+the *successful* drop sequence end-to-end (initgroups → setuid → env restore →
+GUI with `input` group). One-command live test after `sudo make install`:
+run `seekey` on a machine whose `/dev/input/event*` are `root:input 0660`,
+approve the single polkit dialog, then confirm (a) keys are visualized,
+(b) the in-app config menu opens without a second prompt, (c)
+`cat /proc/self/status | grep Groups` inside a child shows the `input` gid.
+
+**Nix:** `package.nix` now runs `make PREFIX=$out install`; `nix build` still
+pins `rev = 625c459…` in `package.nix`, so a fresh build only picks up this
+feature after that rev (or the flake input) is bumped.
