@@ -99,6 +101,13 @@ build deps, builds, installs to `~/.local/bin`, and sets up input permissions:
 ./install.sh --uninstall    # reverse it
 ```
 
+Input access itself is granted through a udev/logind ACL by default, with
+`--input-group` as the permanent fallback. The installer also registers a
+polkit policy: when neither method is available, Seekey asks for a one-time
+`pkexec` authentication and runs with the `input` group for that session.
+The settings menu, live preview, and overlay it starts inherit that access
+without prompting again.
+
 Installation also adds a Seekey desktop entry. On its first launch, choose
 whether future application-menu launches open the settings menu or start the
 key overlay directly. `seekey --config-gui` always opens settings.
